## emulator -help-accel (原始输出, 关键行)



  Use '-accel <mode>' to control how CPU emulation can be accelerated

  when launching the Android emulator. Hardware acceleration is required.

  On Linux, it relies on KVM being installed. On Windows, it relies on

  WHPX. On macOS, it relies on HVF.

  Valid values for <mode> are:



     auto   The default, determines automatically if acceleration

            is supported, and uses it when possible.



     on     Force acceleration. If a hardware CPU accelerator is not

            installed or usable, the emulator will refuse to start and

            print an error message.



     off    UNSUPPORTED: software CPU emulation (TCG) is no longer

            supported, and '-accel off' returns an error unless

            ANDROID_I_WANT_MY_TCG=yes is set in the environment.





